# One token across contexts: the hover background.
# One row for each mode the sum build made.
> value button.hover.backgroundColor across
light/regular  {"colorSpace":"srgb","components":[0.8784,0.9216,0.9882],"hex":"#e0ebfc"}
dark/regular   {"colorSpace":"srgb","components":[0.149,0.2118,0.302],"hex":"#26364d"}
light/compact  {"colorSpace":"srgb","components":[0.8784,0.9216,0.9882],"hex":"#e0ebfc"}
— getModes, resolveValue

# A combination the sum build did not make. The core refuses it and says how to ask for it.
> value button.hover.backgroundColor theme=dark density=compact
error: Mode 'theme=dark density=compact' was not built in collection 'ds'. Name it among the combinations when building, or build every combination with resolveAllToDesignSystem().
— resolveValue

# The same question, late bound: the value under the two contexts, built for no mode.
> value button.hover.backgroundColor how theme=dark density=compact
{"colorSpace":"srgb","components":[0.149,0.2118,0.302],"hex":"#26364d"}
— valueAt
